title: Wi_Start_Day2
---
Widget: Detective is back already?
You: The case is still open, Mr. Widget. And hello.
Widget: But Widget doesn't have anything new to say.
<<wait 1>>
Widget: And hello.
You: See, it’s about me having new questions... not you having new information.
Widget: *thinks*
<<wait 1>>
Widget: OK.
You: Thank you, Mr. Widget.
Widget: *Shyly* Call Widget Widget? MESTER stresses Widget out. As if Widget has done something wrong and is being scolded... *pauses abruptly*
You: *Deep breath* Very well, Widget...
    -> You: Are you expecting to be scolded?
        <<jump Widg_Skipped>>
    -> You: You look like you didn’t sleep well, Widget.
        Widget: *nods* Widget didn’t sleep well. Widget’s sleep showed up at the training ground.
        Widget: *his face darkens* But Widget... couldn’t do it.
        <<jump Widg_Skipped>>
    -> You: You know what, let's talk another time.
        <<stop>>
===
title: Widg_Skipped
---
<<declare $widg_goodhairday to false>>
<<declare $widg_wad_hair to false>>

Widget: *Looks down at his tail* Widget skipped training today.
Widget: Because Widget had a bad hair day.
Widget: Bad hair day makes Widget anxious. Widget can't focus when anxious.
Widget: So Widget...
You: I got the picture, Widget.
You: But I have to say, your hair looks spectacular today.
    <<jump Widg_GoodHairDay>>
===
title: Widg_GoodHairDay
---
<<set $widg_goodhairday to true>>

Widget: *His face brightens up* Widget knows. Want Widget to share his hair routine?
    -> You: *Nod gratefully* You know what, Widget... 
        -> You: Im going you hold you to that offer.   
            You: *Gesture at his shiny hair* If Mr. Waddles really appreciated artistry, he would have asked you to teach him.
            <<jump Widg_Wad_Hair>>
        -> You: Your routine is probably too advanced for me. 
            You: *Gesture at his shiny hair* If Mr. Waddles really appreciated artistry, he would have asked you to teach him.
            <<jump Widg_Wad_Hair>>
    -> You: Let's talk another time.
        <<stop>>
===
title: Widg_Wad_Hair
---
<<set $widg_wad_hair to true>>

Widget: *Bitterly* Mr. Waddles never asked Widget anything. He <i>ordered</i>.
Widget: *Thinks* Mr. Waddles didn't have hair anyway.
Widget: Even Widget couldn't help.
    -> You: What kind of this did Mr. Waddles order you to do?
        Widget: Moving heavy things, *he rubs his shoulder, as if still feeling the weight*
        You: That sounds unfair, Widget. What was the last time you moved a heavy thing for him?
        <<jump Widg_Heavythings>>
    -> You: Did he ever reward you for the things you did for him?
        Widget: *laughs darkly* last time, Mr.Waddles shut the door in Widget's face.
        Widget: Widget was only hoping to use the big makeup table...
        You: That's very rude, Widget. Care to tell me what happened?
        <<jump Widg_Heavythings>>
===
title: Widg_Heavythings
---
Widget: *Thinks* Mr. Waddles asked Widget to move his wagon to the other side of the camp.
<<wait  2>>
    -> You: Pardon?
    -> You: You moved the wagon. Of course.
Widget: *Nods, as if hes remembering*  We stopped to set camp. Boss had accidentally parked Mr. Waddles’ wagon on the other side.
Widget: Said "We need one damned night of proper sleep, for the devil’s sake!"
Widget: *Pauses. Looks uncomfortable for cursing* Mr. Waddles was unhappy. Said practicing trumpet doesn’t feel the same.
Widget: *As fast as he can* o Widget carried his wagon to the spot between Mr. Edward’s wagon and the boss’s. Where he told Widget. Then he left. Closed the door in Widget’s face.
    -> You: That's very rude, Widget. You know what else is rude?
        You: TTaking other people’s things without asking, which Mr. Waddles did...
        Widget: *looks unsure where this is going* Yes?
        You: Tell me Widget..
    -> You: *Nod* Mr. Waddles felt quite entitled to your labor.
        Widget: *Looks sad* He did.
You: Was he feeling entitled to your belongings too?
Widget: *Thinks* Widget... does not have many belongings.
Widget: Widget thinks Mr. Waddles wouldn’t have wanted them if Widget had any.
You: You have that impressing and delicate hair comb.
Widget: *Smiles and reaches for the combs in his hair* Widget got them...
<<jump Widg_Comb>>
===
title: Widg_Comb
---
Widget: *His eyes get wider in horror as he feels the empty space in his hair*
Widget: Oh.
    -> You: Where is your comb, Widget? <<if $comb is false>>
        You: Am I going to find it on the murder scene?
    -> You: I have your comb, Widget. *take the comb our of your suitcase* <<if $comb is true>>
        -> You: Do you need me to tell you where I found it?
        -> You: Do you want me to tell you why I think It's not where it should be?
        -> You: I have so many questions, Widget. Where should I start?
Widget: *eyes wide, his tail shaking constantly* No.
You: You were not friends with Mr. Widget. He wouldn't even invite you inside his wagon... 
    -> You: What would you say if we search the wagon right. now. And find your comb? <<if $comb is false>>
    -> You: \[comb\] Why did I find your hair comb in the now murder scene, then, Widget? <<if $comb is true>>
    -> You: [bluff]\[pocket mirror\] Why are your fingerprints on mirror he always carried? <<if $pocket_mirror is true>>
    -> You: \[pocket mirror|comb\]*Say nothing. Looks at him expectantly* <<if $pocket_mirror is true or $comb is true>>
Widget: *Shaking* Mr. Waddles... stole... Widget's hair comb?
You: Even you yourself don't believe it, Widget.
Widget: No.
<<wait  2>>
Widget: *Shaking sigh* Widget is tired of hiding. Widget cant do this anymore. * takes a deep breath*
<<wait  1>>
Widget: *In one breath* Widget broke Mr. Waddles’ trumpet, but it was an accident. Widget wanted to play it. Widget actually played it... played it better than Mr. Waddles himself...
You: ...
You: Ok, Widget. Slow down...
Widget: *in the same breath*  Widget felt very sad. Widget wanted to make up for it, so Widget skipped training and went to the town and got a brand new trumpet. It was very shiny...
Widget: *pauses* Widget had no idea stuff is so expensive.
Widget: *Almost out of breath* Widget sneaked into Mr. Waddles’ wagon that night to replace the trumpet. Widget can be very sneaky if he wants. Mr. Waddles didn’t even wake up.
Widget: then widget got distracted...
Widget: *pauses, finally out of breath*
    -> You: *softly* It’s OK, Widget. I’m sure it was an accident...
    -> You: *firmly* let me tell you what happened next, Widget...
You: He spotted you, and you got in a fight... And in the heat of the moment, your comb fell off.
You: And you didn’t even notice. You were seeing red, finally so close to the man who did nothing but humiliate you...
Widget: *voice so low it sounds like a scream* NO
Widget: Mr. Waddles was dead when Widget got in! The wagon was quiet. So quiet. Widget got distracted. By stuff.
Widget: Mr. waddles had so many stuff.
Widget: *almost moans* Widget saw Mr. Waddles’ small mirror, the one he always used to correct his tie and his hat and his eyeglasses and his gentleman-y stuff...
Widget: Widget wanted to know how Widget looks in that mirror.
Widget: *cries* Widget was having a good hair day!
You: So your defense, Mr. Widget, is that you ignored a dead body to check yourself out in a mirror?
Widget: *his face twists in pain when you call him Mr* WIDGET DIDN’T IGNORE IT! WIDGET DIDN’T SEE IT!
Widget: Widget only saw the dead Mr. Waddles when he heard Lady Poppet scream...
<<wait  1>>
Widget: Oh.
Widget: *He looks drained* Widget did not want to cause Lady Poppet any trouble.
Widget: But Widget and Lady Poppet didn't kill mr. waddles. *almost begs*
Widget:  Detective needs to understand...
    -> You: *clap your notebook closed* Detective understand very well, Mr. Widget.
        You: I think I just need to talk to lady Poppet to clear some details.
    -> You: *Slowly close your notebook and sigh* Im trying to understand, Widget.
        You: I need to think this through, and also have a chat with your friend.
Widget: *eyes on a point in distance, whispering*
Widget: Widget just wanted to play the trumpet.
<<stop>>
    
===
title: Widg_NoConfession
---
<<declare $widg_saidnothing to false>>

You: Let's see...
    -> You: Were you aware that Mr. Waddles had his trumpet broken?
        Widget: *His eyes widens* Tr... Trumpet? Broken?
        Widget: *Takes a deep breath* Widget is sorry to hear it.
        Widget: *sighs* Trumpets are very very expensive.
        You: ... How do you know that, Widget?
        Widget: B... Boss asks Widget to buy stuff for the circus. When stuff is broken.
        Widget: *explains* Widget can carry heavy things very far.
        Widget: Widget has many responsibilities in the circus. *looks uncomfortable*
        You: Noted, Widget.
        You: Anything you want to share with me?
        Widget: *moves his head left and right* Widget has nothing to share.
        <<set $widg_saidnothing to true>>
        <<stop>>
===